{# Decision template: in continuous mode, who speaks next and to whom, as one choice over the legal (speaker,
   target) pairs among the NPCs near the player. The GameMaster has already decided that someone speaks; it
   suggests who, and this choice decides. Rendered into a decisions request, never into chat messages. Sent when
   dialogue.decisions.useForSpeakerSelection is on; otherwise, or without a usable answer, the GameMaster's own
   pick stands.

   Context set by the game: decision_pairs (key, speakerUUID, speakerName, targetKind, targetUUID, targetName),
   decision_speakers (UUID, name, distance, isVirtual, isPrivateVirtual), conversationParticipants (the UUIDs who
   said or were told one of the newest lines of dialogue), sceneDirection (speaker, target, topic,
   newConversation: the GameMaster's suggestion), crosshairTarget, lastSpeaker, lastDialogueTarget, events,
   maxRecentEvents. The virtual-NPC rules and no self-target are already applied to the pairs. Keys are short and
   numbered per request (s2_tplayer, s2_t5); use p.key as given. There is no none option. Outsiders join only
   when their interjection guidance (the bio's interject_summary) matches; being a companion is not a reason.

   A criterion is one line; profiles and other multi-line decorators belong in the state blocks. #}
{% set ss = get_speaker_selector_settings() %}
{% set tagCompanion = ss.tagCompanion %}
{% set tagInScene = ss.tagInScene %}

[ state last_exchange ]
{% if existsIn(lastSpeaker, "name") and existsIn(lastDialogueTarget, "name") %}
{{ lastSpeaker.name }} spoke last, to {% if lastDialogueTarget.UUID == player.UUID %}{{ player.name }}{% else %}{{ lastDialogueTarget.name }}{% endif %}.
{% else if existsIn(lastSpeaker, "name") %}
{{ lastSpeaker.name }} spoke last, to no one in particular.
{% else %}
No one has spoken yet.
{% endif %}
[ end state ]

[ state recent_dialogue ]
{{ render_template("components\\event_history_compact") }}
[ end state ]

[ state direction ]
{% if sceneDirection.newConversation %}
The scene director wants a new exchange started{% if sceneDirection.speaker %}, and suggests {{ sceneDirection.speaker }}{% if sceneDirection.target %} speaking to {{ sceneDirection.target }}{% endif %}{% endif %}.
{% else %}
The scene director wants the conversation to continue{% if sceneDirection.speaker %}, and suggests {{ sceneDirection.speaker }}{% if sceneDirection.target %} speaking to {{ sceneDirection.target }}{% endif %}{% endif %}{% if sceneDirection.topic %}, about: {{ sceneDirection.topic }}{% endif %}.
{% endif %}
The suggestion is a hint, not a rule.
[ end state ]

[ state nearby ]
{% for c in decision_speakers %}
{% set cinfo = decnpc(c.UUID) %}
{{ cinfo.name }}{% if c.UUID in conversationParticipants %} [IN CONVERSATION]{% endif %}{% if cinfo.isVirtual %}{% if c.isPrivateVirtual %} (virtual: a voice only {{ player.name }} hears){% else %} (virtual: heard by everyone here, but not physically present){% endif %}{% else %} ({{ cinfo.gender }} {{ cinfo.race }}, {{ units_to_meters(c.distance) }}m away){% endif %}{% if tagCompanion and is_follower(c.UUID) %} [COMPANION]{% endif %}{% if tagInScene and ((is_plugin_loaded("SexLab.esm") and is_in_faction(c.UUID, "SexLabAnimatingFaction")) or (is_plugin_loaded("OStim.esp") and is_in_faction(c.UUID, "OStimExcitementFaction"))) %} [IN SCENE]{% endif %}
- {{ render_character_profile("short_inline", c.UUID) }}
- Interjection: {{ render_character_profile("interject_inline", c.UUID) }}
{% endfor %}
Tags: [IN CONVERSATION] said or was told one of the latest lines. {% if tagCompanion %}[COMPANION] travels with {{ player.name }}; that alone is no reason to speak. {% endif %}{% if tagInScene %}[IN SCENE] is physically occupied in an intimate scene and speaks only if addressed by name. {% endif %}
[ end state ]

[ question next choice ]
Decide who speaks next in this scene, and to whom. `recent_dialogue` is the conversation so far, oldest first; `last_exchange` says who spoke last and to whom.
Keep the conversation among the people marked [IN CONVERSATION]. Usually the person the last speaker addressed replies; otherwise another participant answers or reacts to what was said. The last speaker goes again only when no one else has a reason to speak.
Anyone outside the conversation, companions and virtual NPCs included, joins only when they were named, spoken to or directly involved in what just happened, when their Interjection guidance in `nearby` matches what was just said or what just happened, or when the scene director wants a new exchange started and their guidance fits it. A match is specific: the general subject of the scene, being nearby, being a companion or having an opinion is not one. Someone whose guidance is missing or still a placeholder joins only when addressed. A virtual NPC has no body and needs a clear match.
When no conversation is under way, follow the scene director's suggestion if it fits; otherwise choose whoever's Interjection guidance best fits what is happening.
[ criteria ]
{% for p in decision_pairs %}
{% set pv = false %}{% for s in decision_speakers %}{% if s.UUID == p.speakerUUID and s.isVirtual %}{% set pv = true %}{% endif %}{% endfor %}
{{ p.key }}: {{ p.speakerName }} speaks next, to {% if p.targetKind == "player" %}{{ player.name }}{% else %}{{ p.targetName }}{% endif %}{% if pv %} (right only if {{ p.speakerName }} was addressed or {{ p.speakerName }}'s Interjection guidance clearly matches what just happened){% endif %}
{% endfor %}
[ end criteria ]
[ end question ]
